Usage: more [OPTION]... [FILE]...

Display the contents of a file, one screenful at a time.

The more command is a filter for paging through text one screen at a time.

Start modifiers:
  +NUM       display file beginning from line number
  +/PATTERN  display file beginning from pattern match

Interactive commands:
  SPACE/z     display next screenful; z also sets screen size
  ENTER       display next line
  d/s/f/b     scroll, skip lines, skip screens, or go back
  / and n     search and repeat search
  :n/:p/:f    next file, previous file, or file status
  .           repeat previous command
  h or ?      show interactive help
  q           quit

Note: On Windows, more uses the console for interactive paging.

OPTIONS:
  -d, --silent       display help instead of ring bell
  -f, --logical      count logical lines, not screen lines
  -l, --no-pause     suppress pause after form feeds
  -c, --print-over   clear line ends before each page
  -p, --clean-print  do not scroll, clean screen and display text
  -e, --exit-on-eof  exit on end-of-file
  -s, --squeeze      squeeze multiple blank lines
  -u, --plain        accepted placeholder; underlining and bold are already
                     plain
  -n, --lines NUM    number of lines per screenful
  -NUM               same as -n NUM
      --help         display this help and exit
  -V, --version      output version information and exit

EXIT STATUS:
  0  if OK,
  1  if minor problems,
  2  if serious trouble.

WinuxCmd is a Windows implementation of GNU CoreUtils for Linux-Windows developers and AI coding assistants.
